---
description: Secret management rules for storing, rotating, and consuming credentials
globs: [
  "secrets/**",
  "apps/*/secrets/**",
  "packages/*/secrets/**",
  "**/.env",
  "**/.env.*",
  "**/*.tf",
  "**/*.tfvars",
  ".github/workflows/*.yml",
  ".github/workflows/*secret*.yml",
  "**/*.yaml",
  "**/*.yml"
]
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never commit secrets; use secret managers or CI secrets with least-privilege scopes.
- Rotate credentials regularly and on leakage suspicion; automate rotation when possible.
- Avoid long-lived tokens; prefer short-lived, auditable credentials with refresh flows.
- Do not echo secrets in logs, metrics, or error messages; mask outputs in CI.
- Template configs to pull secrets at runtime; do not bake into images or artifacts.
- Restrict access paths (principle of least privilege) and audit secret access.
- Validate secret presence at startup with clear errors; fail fast rather than run degraded.
